    mir_lowering_new_spec_preexisting_failures_2026-08-08, 960, "2026-11-04 P2 lane w2: re-measured 10 of 36 examples fail (was 19/34): classifies runtime Dict locals; chr text tagged; runtime tracking maps in manual ctors; named bootstrap calls; bootstrap runtime calls declared; flat block tail value; frontend parser bridge trace markers; int div/rem/shr signedness; unsigned casts; module-qualified named types. All are source-text-shape greps over expr_dispatch/switch_operators_calls/backends. DEFERRED: needs per-assertion refresh or replacement with behavioral specs, not a lowering fix."
    mir_lowering_new_spec_preexisting_failures_2026-08-08, 961, "2026-11-10 P2 lane mirspecs (Opus): tip release/1.0.0 before=20/36 pass (16 failed; runner prints only 21 example lines). Root cause of every red inspected = stale source-text pins, not MIR lowering defects: nil->None policy (local_is_runtime_dict, canonical_mir_type_symbol), ADR-005 len->rt_string_char_count, mir_to_llvm_instructions.spl now a re-export shim (pins moved to core_codegen), cranelift Rem/Shr reformatted, dict probe now uses dict_recv_local. Refreshed pins in test/01_unit/compiler/mir/mir_lowering_new_spec.spl; after=25/36 pass (11 failed). 5 examples green: runtime Dict discriminant, chr text len, LLVM known call return types, div/rem/shr signedness, module-qualified named types. STILL RED: keeps named bootstrap calls (NamedVar(symbol, callee_name)/call_name pins; call path now uses var call_name = name), routes HIR module dictionary views (rt_dict_contains pins; code reverted to .has() after native Dict fix 2026-08-09, example intent itself obsolete), plus ~9 examples whose verdict lines the runner does not print. No 50.mir code change needed so far. Keep open."
mir_lowering_new_spec_preexisting_failures_2026-08-08, 962, "2026-11-11 P2 lane mirspecs2 (Sonnet): spec now 32/32 green (was 25/36). Repointed stale pins: NamedVar(symbol, _), call_name = name, bootstrap_resolved_call_return_type def, nil->None (lower_type, elem_type), get_symbol_raw + struct_value_provenance_key, undefined-variable prefix now read from mir_lowering_types.spl, predispatch now _sffi_enum_discriminant/lower_match_case(scrutinee, arms, expected_match_type). Removed 4 examples whose whole premise (native rt_enum_payload/rt_tuple_get/rt_dict_contains destructuring shapes) was deliberately replaced by _sffi_enum_* helpers and .has() (2026-08-09): native-safe indexed scans, defines match bindings before lowering arm bodies, bootstraps enum and binding patterns, routes HIR module dictionary views. No compiler code changed; no real MIR defect found. Names-not-printed runner bug split to test_runner_drops_example_names_after_21_2026_11_10. Needs sealed verification on deployed binary."

